            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="249">
                <name>Gujari Mahal Archaeological Museum </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  :   &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://archaeology.mp.gov.in/en-us/Museums/State-Level-Museums/Gujri-Mahal-Museum-Gwalior  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : The museum has a diverse range of exhibits, including sculptures made from terracotta, bronze and stone, paintings, inscriptions, weapons and other excavated material from the Sunga, Gupta and Pratihara dynasties. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#109</styleUrl>
                <Point id="248">
                    <coordinates>78.1705511,26.2341237,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="251">
                <name>Gwalior Zoo </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  :   &lt;br&gt;
                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : This is one of many of the beautiful zoological parks of Madhya Pradesh. This park includes a white tiger, golden pheasants, sambhar, bison, and many other animals. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#109</styleUrl>
                <Point id="250">
                    <coordinates>78.16786098735881,26.209275849999997,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="253">
                <name>Italian Garden </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  :   &lt;br&gt;
                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : an ideal picnic spot for the whole family or a group of school children. The garden adjacent to the palace grounds is built in Italian style. Beautiful fountains, cascading waters make this is a beautiful place. The lush green gardens make the place even more beautiful. It is very closely connected to the Moti Mahal, the former Palace of Scindia dynasty which is now turned into a Government office. The garden is also connected with the Baiji Ki Tal which is a garden along with a beautiful pool. The major attractions here are the boating area and stone fountains add to the beauty and splendor of this park. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#109</styleUrl>
                <Point id="252">
                    <coordinates>-1.369108928180049,50.786511000000004,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
